  "verdict": "Theta(m) = S_m(A) + S_m(A^c) exactly: the divisor-ceiling slack is the divisor supply of the complement support, which for a surviving target is the greedy support of the dual target E-y. Hence Theta(m) - C_m >= sum_{d<=D0} w_d >= 1 unconditionally (the ceiling is never tight), and the branch left open by carry_divisor_bound.py -- ratio C_m/Theta(m) -> 1 -- is exactly equivalent to the dual target's carry being o(Theta). Route closure, not progress on Erdos 257."
